the fourth episode of season eight of  Game of Thrones titled the last of the  Starks was a change of pace after last  week's devastating Battle of Winterfell  but it had its fair share of drama  we finally headed back to King's Landing  to see what Cersei and Euron were up to  now that Aria had killed the night king  the battle for the iron throne could  really begin here are 14 details you  might have missed and warning spoilers  are coming each week during season 8  there have been small adjustments made  to the sprawling opening credits we now  see a new damaged Winterfell the insides  of the castle are in shambles as bodies  burn outside the castle walls  as the survivors celebrate and drink  Tyrion Podrick Brienne and Jaime play a  drinking game it's the same drinking  game we've seen several times throughout  the show first in season one with Shae  and bran and another time he tries and  fails to play it with grey worm and Miss  on day anyone not drinking is  disrespecting all Queen if you look  closely you can see Game of Thrones  creators DB Weiss and David Benioff in  the banquet hall you can spot them as  tormund gives his big speech about Jon  meanwhile Arya doesn't join the others  in the banquet hall she's shooting  arrows by herself  Gendry finds her and proposes asking her  to be the lady of storms end  not long after Daenerys declared him  Lord of storms end she says no and tells  him I don't want to be a lady and I'm  not a lady I never have been That's not  me this is a callback to multiple  moments in the show the first is from  season 1 episode 4 cripples bastards and  broken things when Ned talks to her  about her future as a lady and she says  That's not me  there's another callback to this in  season 7 episode 2 Stormborn  when arya tries to get Nymeria to come  back to Winterfell with her when Nymeria  walks away arya realizes her dire wolf  was meant to roam free and she says bran  tells tyrion that his wheelchair is the  same one that Darren Targaryen builds  for his nephew a hundred and twenty  years ago Darren was the eldest son of  king aegon the third in the books Jon  Snow mentions Darren as a sort of  historical hero of his bran tells Tyrion  I've been shoveling Lannister and what  do I have to show Tyrion starts to  respond power resides where men believe  before being cut off this is a callback  to season 2 episode 3 what is dead may  never die Varys says these exact words  to Tyrion power resides where men  believe it resides it's a trick a shadow  on the wall  Arya and the Hound are riding on  horseback to King's Landing The Hound  says I have business left to be done  he's likely referring to killing his  brother the mountain you know is coming  for you you've always known which could  mean that fans might see the  highly-anticipated Clegane ball very  soon  Arya says so do I a reference to her  kill list on which there are technically  just two names left the mountain and  Cersei Daenerys flee is taken by  surprise when you're on in the golden  company shot down Regal there were hints  throughout the episode that the Dragons  were weak if you look closely you can  see that ray galls wings are full of  holes  both Viserion and regal were brought  down in similar ways one by spear and  one by arrow  Euron uses a giant crossbow called the  scorpion which was invented by Qyburn it  was last seen in the season 7 episode  the spoils of war during the loot train  attack bran uses one against drogon he  hits but fails to kill him  this episode also saw the death of  Masson day with her shocking beheading  before Masson day dies Cersei asks her  if she has any last words she chooses  jerk arse the same words Daenerys says  to her dragons before they breathe fire  this is just one of the many clues  throughout the episode that Daenerys is  going mad like her father King Aerys ii  during the banquet torment teases John  and says what kind of person climbs on a  freakin dragon a madman as Daenerys  listens in the background Varys says he  worries about her mental state and now  Masson day is telling her to burn them  all  just like Aerys did  Daenerys says it's her job to bring down  all tyrants and in this case bringing  down a tyrant might involve destroying  an entire city  Cersei gives the order for Masson day's  execution but the mountain swings the  sword in the pilot episode Ned Stark  says the man who passes the sentence  should swing the sword this is not  something the Lannisters do  Joffrey gives the order to someone else  for Ned's head and speaking of Ned Stark  in the first season Cersei tells Ned  when you play the game of Thrones you  win or you die  this explains why Cersei refuses to  surrender for her she either takes the  throne or loses her life during this  episode  both Daenerys and Cersei are seen in  their full house garb Daenerys was  wearing full Targaryen read at the  celebratory feast a nod to her leaning  into the house words of fire and blood  in the final scene of this episode she's  wearing red and white Cersei is also in  full red for the episode just as  Daenerys is embracing her Targaryen  nature Cersei is back to full Lannister  strength lion necklace and all and not  all Easter eggs are intentional someone  seems to have left a coffee cup on the  table and the feast scene  is there anything we missed let us know  in the comments  [Music]
 

